  "overview": "Barcelona is the capital of Catalonia, set on the Mediterranean coast between the Besòs and Llobregat rivers. It began around 10 BC as the Roman colony of Barcino, and its medieval streets survive in the Gothic Quarter and El Born. The city is best known for Modernisme, the architectural movement that shaped modern Barcelona. Antoni Gaudí's Sagrada Família, begun in 1882, Park Güell, Casa Batlló and La Pedrera are all part of his works listed by UNESCO as World Heritage, and so is the Palau de la Música Catalana, the concert hall designed by Lluís Domènech i Montaner. People come for that architecture, for markets and tapas bars, and for a city with a working port and a run of beaches from Platja de Sant Sebastià to the Fòrum.",
