  "sourceNotes": "FACTS (barcelonaturisme.com, Barcelona's official tourism site, read Oct 2026): Barcino founded around 10 BC as a Roman colony by Augustus, territory between the Besòs and Llobregat rivers; Modernisme, Gaudí and Domènech i Montaner (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/43/history-of-barcelona.html). Sagrada Família begun 1882, Gaudí's masterpiece, part of his UNESCO-listed works, interior columns branch to form a stone forest (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/4727/basilica-of-la-sagrada-familia.html). Park Güell UNESCO-listed, mosaic dragon on the main staircase, main terrace with views of the city and the sea, usually reached on foot from Gràcia (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/755/park-guell.html). Casa Batlló on Passeig de Gràcia, La Pedrera (Casa Milà), Palau de la Música Catalana all UNESCO World Heritage (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/prods/9/especial-patrimonio-de-la-humanidad.html). Palau designed by Domènech i Montaner, built 1905–1908 (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/544/palau-de-la-musica-catalana.html). Carrer Montcada, medieval street of Gothic palaces in El Born (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/390/carrer-montcada.html); Museu Picasso at c/ Montcada 15–23 in a group of palaces (museupicassobcn.cat). La Boqueria on La Rambla, one of the best-known food markets, since 1840 (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/469/mercat-de-la-boqueria.html). Working port; beaches from Platja de Sant Sebastià to the Fòrum (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/1770/sea-and-beaches.html). Capital of Catalonia (spain.info). TIP: Park Güell entry at assigned time, 30-minute grace period, stay as long as you like, no re-entry (parkguell.barcelona/en/buy-tickets). BY PLANE: Josep Tarradellas Barcelona-El Prat Airport; by car from central Barcelona around 20 minutes; R2 Nord train around 20 minutes to Barcelona-Sants; Aerobús around 35 minutes to Plaça de Catalunya (barcelonaturisme.com/wv3/en/page/46/airport.html). BY TRAIN (spain.info/en/route/explore-spain-on-high-speed-trains/): Madrid–Barcelona from 2 hr 30 min non-stop; Barcelona–Seville from 5 hr 18 min; Barcelona–Málaga from 6 hr. Barcelona–Paris (SNCF) and Barcelona–Valencia (Euromed) left out: no consistent official journey time found. BY CAR: Montserrat about one hour via the A2 (spain.info/en/discover-spain/excursions-from-barcelona/). CLIMATE and STAYS unchanged from the previous entry; climate source not re-checked this pass.\nTemperature strip: Average daily high and low in °F.\nPhotos: landscape https://explorajourneys.com/us/en/destinations-globe/med/journeys/cvvbcn-09-v6?id-journey=EP20270305CVVBCN; local https://www.mandarinoriental.com/en/barcelona/passeig-de-gracia/explore (The Hidden World of Cavas Gramona)\nReview 2026-10-03: REVIEW 2026-10-03. CLIMATE: AEMET (Agencia Estatal de Meteorología) climatological normals 1981-2010, station Barcelona Aeropuerto (0076), aemet.es/en/serviciosclimaticos/datosclimatologicos/valoresclimatologicos?l=0076&k=cat; mean daily max (TM) and min (Tm) converted from °C to °F and rounded (e.g. Jan 13.6/4.7 °C = 56/40 °F, Jul 28.0/19.8 °C = 82/68 °F). Previous strip had no named source and its lows did not match AEMET. Barcelona Fabra (0200E) not used: it sits on the Collserola hillside and is not representative of the city. COVER: Sagrada Família Nativity façade at golden hour, Explora Journeys DAM, Barcelona destination-experience asset ESBCN003 (explorajourneys.com/content/dam/explora/pim/destex/med/es/esbcn/esbcn003/ESBCN003.jpg, 7144x4765); same asset family as the previous PHOTO 1 (ESBCN001), loaded dynamically on Explora Barcelona journey pages. HTTP 200 image/jpeg with and without wanderbywilson referer. PHOTO 1: Barcelona from Park Güell's terrace at golden hour, over the city to the sea; Explora Journeys Barcelona port image (explorajourneys.com/content/dam/explora/pim/ports/med/es/esbcn/ESBCN.jpg, 2000x1334), referenced as the Barcelona port image on explorajourneys.com/us/en/destinations-globe/med/journeys/cvvbcn-09-v6?id-journey=EP20270305CVVBCN; 200 image/jpeg with and without referer. PHOTO 2 kept: Mandarin Oriental Barcelona explore page, experience 'The Hidden World of Cavas Gramona' (private tour of a Penedès cava estate ending in a private tasting), image fq35jZdsg7xuCxvAKTTT.jpg confirmed as that experience's image on mandarinoriental.com/en/barcelona/passeig-de-gracia/explore. HIGHLIGHTS: Palau de la Música Catalana designed by Domènech i Montaner, UNESCO-listed (barcelonaturisme.com pages already cited); La Boqueria softened to 'one of the best-known', matching barcelonaturisme.com. TIP re-checked on parkguell.barcelona/en/buy-tickets (30 minutes after ticket time; stay as long as you like; no re-entry). TRAINS re-checked on spain.info high-speed trains page (Madrid from 2 hours 30 minutes, Seville from 5 hours 18 minutes, Málaga from 6 hours). STAYS notes: Mandarin Oriental on Passeig de Gràcia in a former bank building, rooftop terrace and pool at Terrat (mandarinoriental.com; Forbes Travel Guide; Michelin Guide hotel listing). Majestic a block from La Pedrera on Passeig de Gràcia, rooftop terrace La Dolce Vitae with views of the Sagrada Família (majestichotelgroup.com/en/barcelona/hotel-majestic). W Barcelona: Ricardo Bofill's sail-shaped tower at the southern end of Passeig Marítim, Barceloneta (Michelin Guide hotel listing; archello.com project page). No Barcelona hotels in data.js, so images kept.\nTrains: Barcelona-Valencia Euromed about 2 hr 35 to 2 hr 47, 11 a day (Wikipedia Euromed, trenes.com); Barcelona-Girona AVE from 38 min, 27 a day (Trainline).\nThings to do photos (2026-10-03): item 0: https://unsplash.com/photos/sagrada-familia-vaulted-ceiling-in-barcelona-Tja7su9VBTM; item 1: Explora Journeys Barcelona destination experience asset ESBCN004 (explorajourneys.com DAM, same series as the guide's cover ESBCN003); item 2: https://www.mandarinoriental.com/en/barcelona/passeig-de-gracia/explore; item 3: https://www.palaumusica.cat/en (official site, homepage share image); item 4: https://www.flamencopalaudalmases.com/ (Palau Dalmases, Carrer Montcada 20, official site); item 5: Explora Journeys Barcelona destination experience asset ESBCN013 (explorajourneys.com DAM)\nThings to do changes: Item 6 (La Boqueria) replaced with Sant Pau Recinte Modernista: every Boqueria photo found (Unsplash; the market's own site is city-run, so excluded) was a crowded or price-tag-covered stall scene, not luxury quality. Sant Pau has a clean Explora Journeys image. Item 5 (Carrer Montcada) kept; the Museu Picasso is municipally run, so its images were excluded and the photo is the courtyard of Palau Dalmases, a palace on Carrer Montcada, from its own site.\nSant Pau: https://santpaubarcelona.org/en/ (official site: 'A masterpiece by Lluís Domènech i Montaner', former Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau, UNESCO listed, open to visitors) and https://santpaubarcelona.org/en/act-any-domenech/larquitectura-hospitalaria-estudiada-per-domenech-i-montaner/ plus https://santpaubarcelona.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Proposta-recorregut-ENG.pdf (pavilions set among gardens, conceived as a city within the city / garden city). Palau Dalmases at Carrer de Montcada 20: https://www.flamencopalaudalmases.com/\nCover served from /destination-images/barcelona-sagrada-familia.jpg, a 2000px copy of Explora ESBCN003 (original 33 MB).",
