  "overview": "Florence is the capital of Tuscany and the cradle of the Renaissance, a compact city of terracotta roofs and marble churches gathered along the River Arno. Its historic centre has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1982, and nearly everything a first-time visitor wants to see sits within an easy walk. Brunelleschi's dome crowns the cathedral, still the largest masonry dome ever built. The Uffizi holds Botticelli's Birth of Venus, and the Galleria dell'Accademia is home to Michelangelo's David. Across the Ponte Vecchio, lined with jewellers' shops, the Oltrarno keeps a more local feel, with traditional artisans, Renaissance palaces and the Boboli Gardens. People come for the art, then linger over long lunches, Tuscan reds and evenings on the river.",
  "highlightsLabel": "Things to do",
