  "overview": "Lake Como winds through the foothills of the Alps in northern Lombardy, its deep blue water hemmed in by steep green mountains. Bellagio sits on the promontory where the lake's branches meet, with Tremezzo and Varenna facing it across the water. The shores are lined with pastel villages and grand villas, and several of their gardens are open to visitors, from the botanical park at Villa Carlotta to the lakeside loggia at Villa del Balbianello. Life here moves by boat: classic wooden Rivas, water taxis and ferries link the towns, so lunch can be in one village and an aperitivo in another. People come for that slow, lakeside rhythm, for gardens and long lunches by the water, with Milan only about an hour away by car.",
