  "overview": "Lucerne sits on the River Reuss where it meets Lake Lucerne, right in the centre of Switzerland, with Mount Pilatus, the city's own mountain, on the skyline. The old town is made for walking: the Chapel Bridge, the oldest covered wooden bridge in Europe, crosses the river beside its octagonal Water Tower, and painted façades line the squares behind it. Beyond the quays, the lake winds into the Alps like a fjord, and Belle Époque paddle steamers still link its villages to the foot of the mountains. Cogwheel railways and cable cars climb from the shore to summits above lakes and glaciers, so a day can begin with coffee by the river and end high in the Alps. It is the classic Swiss lake city, compact, elegant and surrounded by scenery.",
